

# <type>(<scope>)[!]: <summary>
#
# <body>
#
# <footers>
#
# mfds commit convention. validate_commits.py is its executable form;
# when the two disagree, the validator wins and this file is fixed.
# [Hnnn] = enforced by that rule. No id = judgement, nothing checks it.
# Applies from the commit that added this file; earlier history is
# exempt.
#
# == SUMMARY: line 1 ===================================================
# H001  <type>(<scope>)[!]: <summary>
# H002  at most 72 characters
# H003  line 2 is blank; the summary never wraps
# H005  lowercase after the colon, no final period
# H006  no filler: minor, misc, stuff, things, wip, tweaks, various
# H007  no "+"; two changes are two commits
# H008  first word not past tense or gerund (added, updating, ...)
#       Imperative: "If applied, this commit will <summary>."
#       Identifiers as on disk: ps_09 p_03, ch_14.2, lec_01, exam_01.
#
# == CONTENT: 01_coursework/ ===========================================
# type = facet directory, scope = course directory without NN_
#
# H004  material   01_material/
#       problems   02_problems/
#       exams      03_exams/
# H010  scope required; names an existing course ("just courses")
# H012  every changed path is inside <course>/0N_<type>/
# H011  first word is one of:
#       scaffold   ps_NN or chapter skeleton from source
#       draft      partial work                          -> H013
#       solve      problem complete
#       add        notes, q&a, paper, plan, day file
#       revise     improve content that was already correct
#       correct    fix a mathematical error              -> H030
#       move       rename, renumber, relocate
#       remove     delete
# H013  draft ends with what is open: draft ps_09 p_01 (step 3 open)
#
# == MACHINERY: everything outside 01_coursework/ ======================
# H004  feat       new capability: script, recipe, validator rule,
#                  prompt behaviour
#       fix        tooling gives a wrong result
#       refactor   restructure or rename, behaviour unchanged
#       docs       README.md and STRUCTURE.org prose only
#       chore      .gitignore, bulk mechanical edits, housekeeping
#       revert     undo an earlier commit; body names it
# H020  scope required; the component of at least one changed path
#       ("just commit-scopes"): a script stem, a prompt slug,
#       structure (STRUCTURE.org + its validator), commits (this
#       file + its validator), readme, justfile, gitignore,
#       coursework (mechanical change across courses)
# H021  no 01_coursework/ path unless the scope is coursework
#
# == BODY ==============================================================
# Why, not what; then what you verified (findings, counts).
# H030  required for feat, fix, refactor, revert, correct, and "!"
# H032  wrap at 72; URLs and trailer lines exempt
#
# == FOOTERS ===========================================================
# H031  "!" if and only if a BREAKING CHANGE: footer. Use when a path
#       or CUSTOM_ID that something outside this commit references
#       (org links, image paths, Doom config) now points nowhere;
#       the footer says what must be updated.
#       Co-Authored-By: <model> <noreply@anthropic.com>
#
# Passed through unchecked: Merge, Revert "...", fixup!/squash!/amend!
# H040  pre-push rejects fixup!/squash!/amend! on their way out
